Ps42{
  As the deer pants fro streams of water so my soul pants for you my GOd
  My soul thirsts for God for the living GOd
  When can I go and meet with GOd?
  My tears have been my food day and night while people say to me all day long where is your GOd?
  These things I remember as I pour out my soul
  How I used to go to the house of GOd under the protection of the mighty one
  with shouts of joy and praise among the festive throng

  Why my soul are you downcast? Why so distrubed within me?
  Put your hope in GOd for I will yet praise HIm my savior and my GOd

  My soul is downcast within me
  Therefore I will remember You
  from the land of the JOrdan
  the heights of Herman
  the mounts of Mizar
  Deep calls to deep in the roar of Your waterfalls
  all your waves and breakers have swept over me

  By the day the Lord directs His love
  by night His song is with me.
  A prayer to the God of my life

  I say to God my rock
  Why have you forgotten me?
  Why must I go about mourning oppressed by the enemy?
  My soul suffers mortal agony
  as my foes taunt me saying to me all dya long "Where is your GOd"

  Why my soul are you downcast?
  WHy so distrubed within me?
  Put your hope in God
  for I will yet praise Him, my saviour and my God
}

Ps24{
  The earth is the LORD's and everything in it.
  The earth and all who live in it.
  For He founded it on the and established it on the waters.

  Who may ascend the mountain of the LORD?
  Who may stand in His Holy Place?
  The one with clean hands and pure heart
  who does not trust in idols
  or swear by a false god.

  That person shall receive blessing from the LORD
  and vindication from God their saviour.
  Such is the genration of those who seek Him
  who seek Your face God of Jacob.

  Lift up your head you gates
  be lifted up you ancient doors
  that the King of GLory may come in.
  Who is this king of glory?
  The LORD strong and mighty.
  The LORD mighty in battle

  Lifte up your head you gates
  lift them up you ancient doors
  that the king of glory may come in.
  Who is he, this kings of glory?
  The LORD strong and mighty
  The LORD mighty in battle
  is the king of glory.
}

























